{
  "id": "ss.enemy.boss",
  "name": "Chorus",
  "description": "Not the biggest thing in the hive — the loudest. A seated mass of carapace ringed by six organs that fire in sequence, so the light travels around it like a voice going round a room; that rotation is the whole read. Under the plates is a ring of husk teeth around a vent that has never eaten anything, only shouted. It has no limbs and does not walk, so the rig is in what it does instead: each spine flexes outward as the organ beside it fires and settles as the next takes over, so the sequence runs through the body as well as the light; the plate rings counter-rotate; the teeth turn; the vent breathes. The mass carries pits between the spines and a second course of plate seams, and each spine a bone edge. Gameplay slot unchanged (5:00 boss); body radius still ~38.",
  "tags": ["ss-enemy", "boss"],
  "size": [96, 96],
  "meta": {"radius": 38},
  "parts": [
    {"id": "spine_a", "at": [25.98, 15.0], "rot": 120, "shape": {"kind": "poly", "points": [[-4.2, 2.0], [0.0, -9.5], [4.2, 2.0]]}, "fill": "$husk.dark", "stroke": {"color": "$ink", "width": "hair"}},
